{"records":[{"id":"8p9ss8p6bv","title":"Data for Network Toxicology Reveals Synergistic Mechanism of 4NQO and ethanol in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma","description":"Data for Network Toxicology Reveals Synergistic Mechanism of 4NQO and ethanol in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-05-07T15:12:48.181Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/8p9ss8p6bv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/8p9ss8p6bv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"jianfeng","last_name":"yuan","orcid":"0009-0005-0774-8040"}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grant_id":null}],"categories":["Cancer","Squamous Cell Carcinoma"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"mb38dzj6c2","title":"Data for: Serum IGFBP-1 as a potential biomarker for diagnosis of early-stage upper gastrointestinal tumour","description":"Antibody microarrays detection (AAH-BLG-1000 and AAH-CYT-G4000) to identify candidate biomarkers of esophageal squamous cell carcinoma","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-10-28T13:58:37.01Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/mb38dzj6c2","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/mb38dzj6c2"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yi-Wei","last_name":"Xu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"En-Min","last_name":"Li","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Antibody"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"fvdsbcvtmc","title":"Dr.","description":"LncRNA BCAR4 aggravated proliferation and migration in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma by negatively regulating p53/p21 signaling pathway\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-11-09T19:22:03.977Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/fvdsbcvtmc","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/fvdsbcvtmc"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Chun","last_name":"Fang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Esophageal Cancer","Long Noncoding RNA"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3rdxrp9wj2","title":"RNA modification-related genes illuminate prognostic signature and mechanism in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma. Hui Han.","description":"Original western blotting images produced in the study entitled \"RNA modification-related genes illuminate prognostic signature and mechanism in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-02-13T14:30:18.478Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3rdxrp9wj2","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3rdxrp9wj2"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"HUI","last_name":"HAN","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Life Sciences","Cancer Biomarker"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"f87srd3bz6","title":"PCR","description":"We analyzed mRNA levels of FGF2 and SOX2 in and around esophageal squamous cell carcinoma. Furthermore, they are highly expressed in tumor tissues and promote tumor progression","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-07-23T18:41:34.855Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f87srd3bz6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f87srd3bz6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"wenjingzhang","last_name":"zhang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer Research"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"2fz478mzyn","title":"Supplement to Association of cutaneous immune-related adverse events with improved overall survival among patients with cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma treated with palliative PD-1 inhibition","description":"Supplement to Association of cutaneous immune-related adverse events with improved overall survival among patients with cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma treated with palliative PD-1 inhibition","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-01-31T10:00:32.534Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/2fz478mzyn","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/2fz478mzyn"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Frederick","last_name":"Gibson","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Immunotherapy","Squamous Cell Carcinoma"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3jbktrwtm4","title":"PET/CT deep learning prognosis for treatment decision support in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma","description":"This dataset contains CT, PET, and PET/CT images of patients diagnosed with esophageal squamous cell carcinoma (ESCC). It is released in conjunction with the study: PET/CT deep learning prognosis for treatment decision support in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma. Insights Into Imaging, 2024. DOI: 10.1186/s13244-024-01737-1.\n\nImages of ESCC patients who received two different treatment therapies: namely surgery alone (SA) and surgery followed by postoperative adjuvant chemotherapy (SPOCT), are included. Moreover, the dataset also provides the ESCCPro-SA and ESCCPro-SPOCT models and code, proposed in the aforementioned study, to enable future researchers to replicate the models.\n\nSpecifically, the “ESCC_OA_Data.rar” file consists of two folders, namely “Patients_SA” and “Patients_SPOCT”, which correspond to the data of ESCC patients who underwent each respective therapy.  Each image within the dataset follows a specific naming convention. The initial number in the file name represents the anonymized patient identification (ranging from 1 to 646), followed by the type of image (CT, PET, or PET/CT), and the corresponding image slice number. The final number in the file name is specifically used to differentiate between patients treated with SA (numbers 1-2) and patients treated with SPOCT (numbers 3-4).\n\nPlease cite the reference if using this dataset:\nPET/CT deep learning prognosis for treatment decision support in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma. Insights Into Imaging, 2024. DOI: 10.1186/s13244-024-01737-1","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-06-20T08:51:29.743Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3jbktrwtm4","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3jbktrwtm4"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jiangdian","last_name":"Song","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Gastrointestinal Radiology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hrpkrwt9sc","title":"Heterozygous mutations in SMARCA2 reprogram the enhancer landscape by global retargeting of SMARCA4","description":"Mammalian SWI/SNF complexes are multi-subunit chromatin remodeling complexes associated with an ATPase, either SMARCA4 or SMARCA2. Heterozygous mutations in the SMARCA2 ATPase cause Nicolaides-Baraitser Syndrome (NCBRS), an intellectual disability syndrome associated with delayed speech onset. We engineered human embryonic stem cells (hESCs) to carry NCBRS-associated heterozygous SMARCA2 K755R or R1159Q mutations. While SMARCA2 mutant hESCs were phenotypically normal, differentiation to neural progenitors cells (NPCs) was severely impaired. We find that SMARCA2 mutations cause enhancer reorganization with loss of SOX3-dependent neural enhancers and prominent emergence of astrocyte-specific de novo enhancers. Changes in chromatin accessibility at enhancers were associated with an increase in SMARCA2 binding and retargeting of SMARCA4. We show that AP-1 family member FRA2 is aberrantly overexpressed in SMARCA2 mutant NPCs, where it functions as a pioneer factor at de novo enhancers. Together, our results demonstrate SMARCA2 mutations cause impaired differentiation through enhancer reprogramming via inappropriate targeting of SMARCA4.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-07-30T20:41:17.341Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hrpkrwt9sc","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hrpkrwt9sc"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Diana","last_name":"Hargreaves","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Fangjian","last_name":"Gao","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nicholas","last_name":"Elliott","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot","Immunochemistry"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9nypth6sr7","title":"PRISMA Flow Chart for \"Evaluating the efficacy of targeted muscle reinnervation (tmr) in extremities amputations of pedis squamous cell carcinoma: a comprehensive systematic review, meta-analysis, and meta-regression of functional and pain outcomes\"","description":"This is the PRISMA Flow Chart for \"Evaluating the efficacy of targeted muscle reinnervation (tmr) in extremities amputations of pedis squamous cell carcinoma: a comprehensive systematic review, meta-analysis, and meta-regression of functional and pain outcomes\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-10-09T08:14:12.237Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9nypth6sr7","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9nypth6sr7"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Robin","last_name":"Novriansyah","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Amin","last_name":"Husni","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Rifky","last_name":"Ismail","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yuriz","last_name":"Bakhtiar","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Faiza Rizky Aryani ","last_name":"Septarina","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kevin Christian","last_name":"Tjandra","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nurul Azizah","last_name":"Rahmawati","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sebastian","last_name":"Sudiasa","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mohammad Satrio ","last_name":"Wicaksono","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Meta-Analysis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"sd9yngdx8y","title":"PRISMA Flow Chart for \"Evaluating the efficacy of targeted muscle reinnervation (tmr) in extremities amputations of pedis squamous cell carcinoma: a comprehensive systematic review, meta-analysis, and meta-regression of functional and pain outcomes\"","description":"This is the PRISMA Flow Chart for \"Evaluating the efficacy of targeted muscle reinnervation (tmr) in extremities amputations of pedis squamous cell carcinoma: a comprehensive systematic review, meta-analysis, and meta-regression of functional and pain outcomes\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-10-09T10:46:07.984Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/sd9yngdx8y","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/sd9yngdx8y"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Robin","last_name":"Novriansyah","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Amin ","last_name":"Husni","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yuriz","last_name":"Bakhtiar","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Faiza Rizky Aryani ","last_name":"Septarina","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kevin Christian","last_name":"Tjandra","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nurul Azizah","last_name":"Rahmawati","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sebastian","last_name":"Sudiasa","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mohammad Satrio ","last_name":"Wicaksono","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Meta-Analysis"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":137812,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":162,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":137812,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":137095,"restricted":69,"embargoed":648},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2300},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1336},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":679},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":478},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":442},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0m